<caml:Content xmlns:caml="http://lc.ca.gov/legalservices/schemas/caml.1#"><p>As used in this chapter:</p><p>(a)<span class="EnSpace"/>“Artificial intelligence” means an engineered or machine-based system that varies in its level of autonomy and that can, for explicit or implicit objectives, infer from the input it receives how to generate outputs that can influence physical or virtual environments.</p><p>(b)<span class="EnSpace"/>“Generative artificial intelligence” or “GenAI” means an artificial intelligence system
						  that can generate derived synthetic content, including text, images, video, and audio that emulates the structure and characteristics of the system’s training data.</p><p>(c)<span class="EnSpace"/>“Person” means a natural person.</p><p>(d)<span class="EnSpace"/>“Report” means the report to the Governor required by Executive Order No. N-12-23.</p></caml:Content>